# Evidence and results are large, machine-generated, and content-addressed.
# Committed results live under results/ as curated artifacts only.
/results/**/raw/
/evidence/
*.blob
# P0-10's census evidence store (default `results/census/evidence/`). None of the three
# patterns above reach it: `/evidence/` is root-anchored, `raw/` is the wrong leaf name, and
# a blob is addressed by a bare 64-hex digest with no extension at all. Left untracked but
# un-ignored, verbatim third-party response bytes sat one `git add -A` from being committed
# to a public repo — including `instructions` prose written imperatively at a model. See
# results/census/README.md.
/results/**/evidence/

# Sandbox scratch
/sandbox-scratch/
*.upper/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Local config and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/config.local.*
# F-08's *rendered* cloud-init user-data (scripts/vm/user-data.template is the committed
# half). The rendered copy embeds one contributor's SSH public key, i.e. per-host state, not
# project state. scripts/vm-provision.sh writes it under $MCP_VM_DIR, outside the repo, so
# this line is belt-and-braces — but the template's promise that the rendered form is never
# committed should be structural rather than only a comment inside the template.
/scripts/vm/user-data
/scripts/vm/seed-src/

# Rust build artifacts
/target/
